> I took a quick look at your code, and it appears like the number of rows in the "y" array is 90 while the number of rows in the "occ.covs" is 193. This is where the discrepancy is arising. For a multi-season spatial occupancy model, the data needs to be in the form of a list, and the number of rows in covariates in the list must match up with the number of rows in "y". Take a look at the example in the vignette <https://doserlab.com/files/spoccupancy-web/articles/spacetimemodelshtml#data-structure-and-example-data-set> to see the format that is required.
>
> Kind regards,
