Dear Joaquin,

fit is good, since the Bayesian p-value is nowhere near the extremes of 0 and 1 (which would indicate a model that fits too well or not, respectively). But adding informative detection covariates may yield more precision in your occupancy estimates. And of course, spOccupancy copes with missing values (provided they occur at exactly the same places in the response as in an observational covariate for detection).

Best regards  --- Marc

